  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nAs mentioned in the short term discussion, hot conditions continue \nSunday through at least early next week. Ridging shifts further \nnorth Sunday, then gradually shifts eastward towards the Lower \nMississippi and Tennessee Valleys Monday. This will bring back a \nslight increase in moisture, most notably in the eastern half of the \nforecast area. High temperatures will continue to hover around from \nthe upper 90s to around 102 degrees through Tuesday, and heat index \nvalues may again approach or exceed Heat Advisory criteria during \nthis time depending on location. The main message remains that \nsummer is not over and to continue to practice heat safety. \n\nOutside of some seabreeze showers or thunderstorms each day in the \nlate afternoons, mainly dry conditions continue across South Central \nTexas.",
